-- ── story 4-6a: client consignment compliance ────────────────────────────
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the order_consignment_records table, the clients,
-- shipments and vendor_returns columns and the five indexes — made IF NOT
-- EXISTS by hand, the 6-2a lint) and hand-amended: the fail-fast guard, every
-- CHECK (drizzle-kit is blind to them), the immutability trigger, the RLS
-- policy with the 0041 client clause, the mail and contacts widening and the
-- post-migration probes (`bun run db:generate` afterwards reports "No schema
-- changes").
--
-- What changes:
--  * `order_consignment_records` (A1) — one version of a client order's brand
--    tax document and e-way bill; one live version per order; immutable but
--    for its ending columns and a one-way dispatch stamp.
--  * `clients.consignment_document_rule` (A2) — `b2b` (a constant default:
--    the add is metadata-only), `all` or `high-value`.
--  * `shipments.compliance_exception` (A3) — a device handover that left
--    without the documents. Its CHECK is added NOT VALID (the 0102 / 0116
--    precedent: `shipments` can be large); every existing row is NULL in a
--    column this migration adds, so it holds by construction. Its index is
--    IF NOT EXISTS so a large table can be pre-built CONCURRENTLY (DEPLOY §5).
--  * `vendor_returns.declared_value_paise` (A4) — validated (a small table).
--  * `email_messages` gains `client-documents-needed`; `client_contacts`
--    gains `consignment.documents-needed` (A5, A47).
--
-- No VALIDATE runs here (A48 as corrected by drift D2): the migrator applies
-- the whole pending set in ONE transaction (guide §3), so a VALIDATE beside an
-- ADD would scan under the ADD's ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock. The two email_messages
-- CHECKs are re-added NOT VALID over a superset (asserted below); their
-- VALIDATEs and the shipments one are a post-deploy step (DEPLOY §5, PENDING).
-- 0119 (4-9a) and 0120 (4-10a) drop and re-add the mail and contacts CHECKs
-- BY NAME — the names are a contract. No orders index (drift D3: 0104's
-- accepted and 0116's ready-to-dispatch indexes serve the worklist).
-- No foreign keys (IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE §3). Additive only: no backfill.

-- ── 0. fail-fast: already applied, or out of order ──────────────────────
DO $$
BEGIN
	IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'order_consignment_records') THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0118: order_consignment_records already exists — this migration has already been applied.';
	END IF;
	IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'order_packs') THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0118 is out of order: order_packs does not exist — 0117 must be applied first.';
	END IF;
END $$;
